; Paint's strings, in English: the program is built with these, and a
; translation in LOCALE:Catalogs/<language>/programs/Paint.catalog
; stands in for them. A text written by RawDoFmt takes its values in
; order: a translation keeps them so.
#version 1
;
; The menus.
MSG_MENU_PROJECT (1//)
Project
MSG_MENU_NEW (//)
New...
MSG_MENU_QUIT (//)
Quit
MSG_MENU_EDIT (//)
Edit
MSG_MENU_UNDO (//)
Undo
MSG_MENU_REDO (//)
Redo
MSG_MENU_CLEAR (//)
Clear
MSG_MENU_SWAP (//)
Swap Colours
MSG_MENU_VIEW (//)
View
MSG_MENU_ZOOM_IN (//)
Zoom In
MSG_MENU_ZOOM_OUT (//)
Zoom Out
MSG_MENU_ACTUAL_SIZE (//)
Actual Size
MSG_MENU_GRID (//)
Grid
MSG_MENU_BRUSH (//)
Brush
MSG_MENU_ROUND (//)
Round
MSG_MENU_SQUARE (//)
Square
MSG_MENU_SIZE (//)
Size
MSG_MENU_SMALLER (//)
Smaller
MSG_MENU_LARGER (//)
Larger
MSG_MENU_SETTINGS (//)
Settings
MSG_MENU_OWN_SCREEN (//)
Own Screen
;
; The tools' hints.
MSG_TOOL_FREEHAND (//)
Freehand: a line where the pointer goes
MSG_TOOL_DOTS (//)
Dotted freehand: the brush where the pointer is
MSG_UNDO_HINT (//)
Undo the last change
MSG_REDO_HINT (//)
Make the change undone again
MSG_ZOOM_IN_HINT (//)
Show the picture larger
MSG_ZOOM_OUT_HINT (//)
Show the picture smaller
;
; The line under the picture: its size, the zoom and the brush, and
; while painting where the pointer is.
MSG_STATUS (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld
MSG_STATUS_AT (//)
%ld x %ld   %ld:1   brush %ld   at %ld, %ld
;
; The new picture's window.
MSG_NEW_TITLE (//)
New Picture
MSG_WIDTH (//)
Width
MSG_HEIGHT (//)
Height
MSG_OK (//)
OK
MSG_CANCEL (//)
Cancel
;
; Requesters.
MSG_CHANGED (//)
The picture has changed.\nDiscard it?
MSG_CHANGED_BUTTONS (//)
Discard|Cancel
MSG_NO_PICTURE (//)
There is no memory for a picture\nof %ld by %ld pixels.
MSG_NO_UNDO (//)
That change was too large to keep:\nit cannot be undone.
MSG_NO_OWN_SCREEN (//)
No screen of its own could be opened.
;
; What the shell is told.
MSG_NOLIBRARY (//)
No %s\n
MSG_NOSCREEN (//)
No screen - no display\n
MSG_NOMEMORY (//)
No memory for the window\n
MSG_BADSCREEN (//)
SCREEN is OWN or DESKTOP\n
